      "line": 63,
      "severity": "blocker",
      "rule": "ARCHITECTURE",
      "summary": "Synchronous refresh closes loop-bound governed clients on a new event loop and detaches the live runtime before cleanup succeeds.",
      "diagnosis": "Governed HTTPX async clients are owned by the event loop that used them. The public synchronous refresh creates a fresh loop with asyncio.run for their shutdown. A loop-bound close failure leaves _container cleared, so a previously usable runtime becomes uninitialized. The new async refresh test explicitly asserts cleanup on the caller loop, but the sync refresh test uses only AsyncMock.",
      "evidence": "RuntimeManager.initialize(refresh=True) calls _detach_if_current(current) then asyncio.run(_shutdown_container(detached)) at lines 60-64; ObservedResources._close_all awaits each owned async resource aclose() on the current loop; test_async_refresh_closes_loop_bound_owner_on_caller_loop asserts that loop identity.",
      "correction": "Before detaching, route sync refresh to an owner-loop-safe shutdown transaction or reject it when governed async owners exist, preserving the live container and directing callers to ensure_initialized_async(refresh=True). Add a real loop-bound owner regression for the sync entry point."
    }
